Hi,

There is a new version of the linux Tokenring support available from
linux3.cc.kuleuven.ac.be:/pub/Linux and ftp.cs.kuleuven.ac.be:/pub/unix/linux.
Filename is  TokenRing.patch-1.1.64.gz. Due to a change in our computing
centre's network, the address aix13ps2.cc.kuleuven.ac.be will soon be invalid.
Please use linux3.cc.kuleuven.ac.be instead.

Most important changes :

   + Better detection and configuration of the adapter.
	+ Support for alternate address of the adapter.
	+ Support for 2 adapters (untested).
	+ Bug fixes to source routing code.
	+ Cleanup of the driver code.

Most boards based on IBM's TROPIC chipset should work now. The following boards
are known to be working with the driver :

IBM Token Ring Adapter II
IBM Token Ring 16/4 Adapter
IBM Token Ring Adapter/A 
IBM Token Ring 16/4 Adapter/A
HyperRing Classic 16/4

Boards which use the TI chipset or busmastering DMA won't work with the current
driver. However someone is working on a driver for the IBM busmaster adapters.

Some notes on the driver itself:

+ The driver and support routines are distributed as a patch against 1.1.64. I 
  haven't tested the patch against other kernel versions. I never have tested
  the driver in a 1.0.x kernel.

+ Most IBM token ring boards want I/O address 0x220 or 0x224. This is also the
  address range default used by soundblaster cards. Be aware of this when you
  install a board in a soundblaster equipped machine.

+ Source rounting is still very alpha. I.e. it works for some people, it 
  doesn't for others. This needs to be fixed before the driver can leave the
  alpha state. Anyone with good knowledge of source routing is welcome to look
  at the code.

I would like to thank Yoshinori Tahara, Issam Chehab and Dominique Duvivier for
their testing and fixes of the source routing code. I would also like to thank
David Morris for cleaning up the code and adding support for the alternate I/O
address and 2 adapters.

Peter.

