I have finally fixed the HTML version of the book, "Linux Installation 
and Getting Started", available via the World Wide Web. The Web pages 
no longer access button images from the UK (they have been replaced with 
text strings, [Next], [Previous], etc.), and my address appears after 
each page, as opposed to Per Abrahamsen's, who did the original HTML
translation. 

The URL for this book is
	http://sunsite.unc.edu/mdw/LDP/gs/gs.html

Note that Sunsite's WWW access can be slow during peak hours; 
I have placed a tar file containing the HTML tree for the book
on the FTP site mentioned below. Feel free to grab it and
make it available on your own Web server. For most people,
it's easier to download and print the book; but the HTML
version is a good way to browse it.

For those who don't know, this is a (more or less) complete
installation and novice guide to the Linux system. It's available
for free via the Internet, and from a number of publishing
companies. You can also FTP copies of the book, in various formats,
for printing from 	
	sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/docs/LDP/install-guide
See the README file there for details.

The current version of the book is 2.1.1; I'm about to release a
revised 2.2.1. Unfortunately, the HTML version of the book still 
corresponds to version 2.0. This is because I've had no time to do 
the conversion from LaTeX to HTML; once I release 2.2.1 perhaps I'll 
find a volunteer to help. 

Cheers,
mdw


