 Hi,

 I am happy to announce the release of zlibc-0.5.

 Unlike the previous version, this one works with libc.4.6.20.so

 Zlibc is a library patch that allows executables to uncompress their
datafiles on the fly. No kernel patch, no recompilation of these
executables and no recompilation of the binaries is needed. Using gzip
-9, a compression ratio of 1:3 can easily be achieved! (See examples
below). This program has (almost) the same effect as a (read-only)
compressed file system.

 Where to find it:
 =================
 There is a binary and a source distribution, called
zlibc-0.5.bin.tar.gz and zlibc-0.5.scr.tar.gz
 On sunsite, they are now in pub/Linux/Incoming, and their permanent
locations are (will be):
 sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/libs
 tsx-11.mit.edu:/pub/linux/binaries/libs
 tsx-11.mit.edu:/pub/linux/sources/libs
 ftp.imag.fr:/pub/Linux/ZLIBC/zlibc

 How to install it:
 ==================

 The source distribution is the recommended way of installing zlibc,
as it contains a configure script and an automated install
script. Moreover, the source distribution is not tied to any
particular version of libc. To install from source, type 'tar xfzvvp
zlibc-0.5.src.tar.gz', and read zlibc-0.5/INSTALL.linux for further
instructions.

 To install the binary version, type 'cd / ; tar xfzvvp zlibc-0.5.bin.tar.gz',
and read /usr/doc/zlibc/INSTALL.linuxbin for further instructions.
The binary version uses libc.4.6.20.so

 New in this release:
 ====================

 The following new features have been introduced:

 * zlibc works now with the new 4.6.20 library.
 * There is now a limited support for writing to compressed files. It
is possible to:
  - have the new files created as compressed.
  - append data to compressed files.
  - uncompress files in place before writing to them.
 See the manual page zlibrc.so.5 for details.
 * On Linux, zlibc is now compatible with strace.
 * It is now possible to generate the "compiled in" defaults from the
zlibrc.sample file.
 * Safer default zlibrc file.


 How it works:
 =============

 This package patches the "open" function (and other similar system
call functions) in the shared library. You don't need to have the
sources of the shared library, the binary is patched directly.

 On Linux, this package _should_ work with every .4 shared library
(tested on 4.3.3, 4.4, 4.4.1, 4.4.4, 4.5.26, 4.6.20). This is because
it patches the jumptable, and the jumptable should remain constant for
the same major release number (4) of the shared library.

 On SunOs, this package uses the LD_PRELOAD/LD_LIBRARY_PATH mechanism
to redirect the dynamic linker to use the relevant functions of
uncompress.o instead of the shared library. Thus, it should work with
every release of the shared library (tested on libc.so.1.7). On SunOs,
you don't need to be superuser to install this package.


