These changes are archived on ftp.emlist.com:pub/kchanges.

Updated CREDITS
Added Adaptec AHA274X/284X and UltraStor 14F/34F to config.in turned
	off by default.
cdu31a driver no longer supports DMA because it's too slow.
cdu31a can read 2048 bytes (more efficient, but cannot execute files
	off cd), will support XA disks, will treat multi-session disks
	as if partitioned, and supports reading of raw audio tracks.
Changes to serial driver:
	* serial.c (rs_ioctl, get_lsr_info): Added patch suggested by Arne
		Riiber so that user mode programs can tell when the
		transmitter shift register is empty.
	* tty_ioctl.c (wait_until_sent): Added debugging printk statements
		(under the #ifdef TTY_DEBUG_WAIT_UNTL_SENT)  
	* serial.c (rs_interrupt, rs_interrupt_single, receive_chars,
		change_speed, rs_close): rs_close now disables receiver
		interrupts when closing the serial port.  This allows the
		serial port to close quickly when Linux and a modem (or a
		mouse) are engaged in an echo war; when closing the serial
		port, we now first stop listening to incoming characters,
		and *then* wait for the transmit buffer to drain.  

		In order to make this change, the info->read_status_mask
		is now used to control what bits of the line status
		register are looked at in the interrupt routine in all
		cases; previously it was only used in receive_chars to
		select a few of the status bits.
Added module capability to msdos and umsdos filesystems.
Oops, we were allowed to change the owner of our input under any
	circumstances.  A little too liberal (seee 1.1.59).
Oops, forgot to mark an inode as dirty.
Allow "conv=m" for file conversion.
Oops, swapped uid and gid in setting popt structure.
Use 512 byte blocks instead of 1024 because it fits better with DOS's
	cluster alignment.
Remember when we fixed the readdir stuff?  Also fix it in sysv filesystem.
Be more intelligent about what to readahead into the msdos fs's cache.
umsdos sets the readahead flag as needed.
umsdos now uses generic mmaping.
Some DEC Alpha assembly language functions added.
A whole bunch of ksyms added so that we can use modular filesystems.
Set the minimum number of free pages dynamically.
Break the DNS resolver by matching on the IP address too soon.
If we don't have a gateway, no need to broadcast past it.
Check for null sockets in sock_wake_async().
--
