This is the first release of PCMCIA SCSI stand-alone device driver for
Bus Toaster card made by New Media Corporation.
 
This release supports only Intel PCMCIA controllers (i82365 and the like).
It does not support TCIC, Data Book, Vadim or any other non-Intel chips.
 
This device driver is stand-alone. That is it works without card manager
and the card should be present at the boot time with all SCSI devices
attached - pretty much like any other SCSI host driver for Linux.
 The first thing card manager (by David Hinds) does is resetting PCMCIA
so Bus Toaster will stop working after cardmgr is fired up.
Most likely you should disable all other PCMCIA support or just don't
run cardmgr when using this version of the driver. Cardmgr support will
be implemented in the future version.
 
It is known to work with Linux-1.5x .
My computer is NEC Versa E and I didn't test it with any other laptops.

Source files bus_toaster.c and bus_toaster.h and sample of hosts.c and
		Makefile can be found at:

	lamont.ldeo.columbia.edu: pub/linux/bus_toaster-1.5.tgz

Please read included README.txt file before responding.

Gennady  <gennady@ldeo.columbia.edu>


