Hi Folks,

I upgraded to X11R6 and nothing worked anymore. All my nice utils were gone.
So I started to recompile everything.

The first thing I wanted was fvwm, which compiles out of the box if you have
libXpm. So I took libXpm-3.4c and tried to compile it, which failed.

So I produced a shared libXpm manually. Now fvwm compiled straight out of
the box.

The next thing I really missed was ImageMagick (I missed xv, too, but I
wasn't planning to release it, unless you overflow my mailbox with pleas ;)

So I made a shared libjpeg from the latest IJG JPEG sources and I took the
latest libtiff from sgi.com and made a shared library of it, and finally I
made ImageMagick with a shared libMagick.

If you ever tried to make ImageMagick, then you know that the binaries get
600+ k, and because I have never seen any shared ImageMagick binaries
around, I took my time to do it, and now the programs are 20k each, except
display, which is 150k now (was 800k) !

ImageMagick is a memory hog, but it's a fine image manipulation, display and
conversion tool. Give it a try !

ImageMagick is v3.3 and compiled for X11R6.

I uploaded everything at sunsite.

Felix
