Mosaic (TueV) 2.4.2 + X11R6 + term + HDF

This is an another Mosaic port. This is Mosaic (TueV) 2.4.2
that has many additional features added as well as many
bug fixes (check out README-2.4.2) over NCSA's version.
This one is compiled with X11R6 libraries and with term
support. As a bonus I've thrown in HDF support for browsing
scientific data sets. Good place to check this out is a Mosaic
Demo page.

WARNING! This beast is huge so if you have less then 16 Mb,
you may not want to run it.

Few words about this port.  First of all, it is compiled with
X11R6 libraries and statically linked with Motif 1.2.2.
Also term support is added and linked with _shared_ libtermnet
2.2.5, so you can use this binary either over SLIP/PPP or term
connection. HDF library support  is included so you can browse
some scientific data sets out there. Just be warned, they tend
to be quite large in size.

The files: mailcap, mime.types, documents.menu, go to
/usr/X11R6/lib/X11/Mosaic or you may try to override this by
setting up environmental variable MOSAICDIR
(so in this case MOSAICDIR is /usr/X11R6/lib/X11/Mosaic).
The default home page is http://www.uni-tuebingen.de,
the documentation directory is defined in file://localhost$(MOSAICDIR)/Docs.
The file app-defaults.color should be renamed to Mosaic and put in to
appropriate place (/usr/X11R6/lib/X11/app-defaults).

Thats about it, send bug reports to appropriate sites.
Happy WWW-netting.

