With the exception of a patch to fix cutting and pasting in X11 when
the selection buffer is 4k (which I just sent off to Linus this
morning), as of 1.1.61 I've fixed all known, reproduceable bugs that
have been reported to me regarding the tty drivers, including the serial
driver.

However, it's said that if a program is being used, it always has at
least one bug, so a programmers job is never done.  Since the 1.2
release is imminent, it's important that people let me know if there are
any major bugs outstanding in the drivers.

While bug reports of any kind are welcome, I'd really appreciate it if
people could at least try the following:

=====================

1.  Try very hard to figure out how to reliably reproduce the bug.
Often, I simply can not reproduce it on my system, because I don't have
the same hardware, or software setup.  If you are using some complicated
program that's not working right, please try to take the sources to that
program and reduce it down to an easily demonstrated test case, and send
me that test case program.

2.  Please give me enough information about your system.  Especially if
it's a problem related to your serial ports, *please* gather and report
at least the following pieces of information:

	* How many serial ports you have; and what ports and irq's they use.
	* What RS-232 lines does your serial port support, especially
		paying attention to the following: DCD, RTS, CTS
	* What RS-232 lines does your serial *cable* support?
	* What RS-232 lines does your device (modem, terminal) support?
		(Often times, people who gather this information will
		manage to successfully debug their problem by themselves...)
	* What version of the kernel are you running?
	* What software are you using to access your serial ports?
		(List *all* of them.  If you are using Taylor UUCP,
		pppd, and supprort incoming dialup lines using mgetty,
		tell me so!  Don't just tell me that UUCP is broken....)
	* How is your software configured?  Send me configuration files,
		if you can, and documentation so I can understand the
		configuration files, if it's a wierdo package.  (It's
		amazing how many kernel bugs turn out to be a
		misconfigured gettytab....)

3.  If you think that a recent change to the kernel is causing the
problem, please state the last kernel version you tried that worked, and
the most recent kernel version where things failed.  The worst offenders
are the ones that say, "something you changed recently is breaking
stuff!" --- with no mention of what kernel version they're using.  Then
I ask, and it comes out that they used to be using 1.0.9, and they're
trying to switch to 1.1.31.  (This was back when the latest kernel
patchlevel was 1.1.52 or so....)

Please, please, please.  It really helps if you can first try the most
recent kernel release, and see if that fixes the problem.  If it
doesn't, please try to narrow down the kernel patchlevel where things
broke for you.  At the very least, tell me what kernel patchlevels you
tried....

=====================

These days, I'm extremely pressed for time, so if you're having bugs
with the tty drivers or the serial driver, I'd really appreciate it if
you could do as much work as possible tracking down the problem before
you contact me.

At the same time, however, I *do* want to get feedback about how people
think things are going, in preparation for the 1.2 release.  So even if
you can't give me much information, please let me know if you're having
problems.  But if you do have the time, skills, and knowledge to do some
investigating first before sending in your bug report, I'd really
appreciate it.

Thanks....

						- Ted





