============================================================================
VideoteXt V0.2 for Linux                      Copyright (c) 1994 Martin Buck
============================================================================

Excerpt from the README:

With this program and the included videotext-driver it's possible to read
and display videotext-pages from a videotext-card. The program can be used
either on an Color/BW-ASCII-terminal or with the X-window system.
Unfortunately, there are no special features at the moment, since the
current implementation's main purpose is to demonstrate how to use the
videotext-driver. Future versions will (hopefully) be able to use TOP-Text,
handle a hotlist and load/save/print videotext pages.

At the moment, the only supported interfaces are the one published in the
german computer-magazine c't 11/91, p. 228 and one interface I developped on
my own (this interface makes it possible to connect the videotext-chipset
in a VCR to the parallel port of a PC). Since I don't have any information
on other videotext-interfaces, I can't support them at the moment. But if
you have an unsupported interface, please tell me; otherwise I will probably
never support it.

To be able to install the driver you have to add some symbols to your
kernel-sources at the moment. I hope that starting with Linux 1.1.64 you
will be able to load the driver without recompilation.

NOTE FOR USERS OUTSIDE OF EUROPE:
I don't know if there are TV-stations outside of europe which send
videotext. Therefore I don't know if this program will be of any use for
foreign users. If you use this program outside of europe, *please* send me
e-mail telling me where you are and what TV-station broadcasts videotext. If
there is enough interest, I will upload this program to sunsite.

