Content-Type: text/plain; charset=ISO-8859-1
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Keywords: libg++, C++, library

This is the a.out binary release of the official GNU C++ library
2.6.1 for Linux. You have to install gcc 2.6.2 or above and 
libc 4.6.20 or above to use it. Please don't use it with older gcc
or libc.

There are a few major changes:

1. The g++ header files are moved to /usr/include/g++.
2. There are shared C++ libraries for ELF.
3. CursesW.o is in libcurse++.a instead of libg++.a.
4. librx.a in the part of the Linux C library. No need to use the one
   in libg++ 2.6.1.

Iostream is now back to libg++.a. But you have to use it with libc
4.6.19 or above.

It is on tsx-11.mit.edu under pub/linux/packages/GCC and sunsite.unc.edu
under pub/Linux/GCC.  It is compressed with gzip 1.2.4.

I strongly discourage compiling libg++ 2.6.1 yourself unless you know
what you are doing. I have made many modifications/bug fixes. I have
to work around the gcc bugs. I hope my changes can be merged in the
next libg++ 2.6.x or 2.7.x and gcc gets fixed. But I don't know what
will happen.

The file list:

1. libg++-2.6.1.tar.gz

  REQUIRED. g++-include, libg++.a, libiostream.a, libcurses++.a,
  libiberty.a and genclass. It is libg++ 2.6.1. To install

  su root
  rm -f /usr/g++-include /usr/include/g++
  cd /
  zcat libg++-2.6.1.tar.gz | tar xvvf -
  ln -s /usr/include/g++ /usr/g++-include

H.J.
hjl@nynexst.com
11/12/94

