Keywords: Linux, distribution, nuucp, zmodem, downloads, bbs, Switzerland,
	Slackware

As a service to Linux users in Switzerland not having easy retrieval of
patches and new kernel releases, we allow guest users to download Linux
from our system based in Colombier (Neuchatel).

We do not keep everything and we limit ourselves to a rather simple
Slackware copy, with some utilities and documentation. If you want to
install Linux for the first time, you better buy a CD-ROM with everything
needed on it. Due to the phone cost structure in Switzerland, buying
a CD drive and a CD-ROM may be cheaper than downloading online.

Of course, there is no cost, except the mentionned PTT taxes, to get the
software. There is also currently no support and no warranty about the
content and availability for obvious reasons. There is some delay between
the availability of Linux software and its presence on our site.

The archive has also some other files on it (For example Amiga NetBSD,
diverse UNIX sources, and Aminet).

We ask guest users not to call from 17h-19h, since this is sometimes
overloaded even for ALPHANET NF members. There is an automated system
which enforces drastic limits in some cases. Preferred hours are
22h to 01h and, of course, full-tax time (08h-17h).

If you do not live in Switzerland, the time is given in GMT+1 (MET).

Phone number: (038) 41.40.81  (within Switzerland. Outside dial +4138414081)

a) Guest login

Enter the 'guest' login name, accept the disclaimers, choose a
terminal, identify yourself and select menu item 9, then menu item
2. This is a curses(3X) interface to download files. Then select the
files you want. You will receive them via ZMODEM.

b) nuucp

The file list is in ~nuucp/ls-laR.gz. The linux software is in
/share/archives/linux.

The modem allows connections upto 14'400 (V32bis).

This service is maintained by ALPHANET NF, a not-for-profit association
active in the telecom domain. Send comments about the archive to
fileadm@alphanet.ch, and for to the association to admin@alphanet.ch

