Hi,

I just uploaded PBMSCAN 1.0 to sunsite.unc.edu and ftp.gwdg.de.

PBMSCAN is a scanning program for the Logitech ScanMan 32 scanners
(the 256 will be supported as soon as someone gives me one for testing ;-)).

It needs the Logitech scanner driver of A.Beck and T.Faehnle and 
writes a PBM or PGM file of the scanned image to its standard output.
PBMSCAN can be used most effectively in pipes with the PBM tools.
It was tested with the binary distribution of the NetPBM package under 
Linux 1.0.9.

To view the images you will need xli or xv. I strongly recommend xli,
because it is MUCH faster than xv in most cases.

PBMSCAN supports inverted output, doubling of scan lines for use with
the low-resolution g3 fax format and conversion of b&w images to 
grayscale with a 2x2 matrix (gives 5 gray shades with 1/2 of the
original resolution). 

This program is a lot faster than the gifscan demo that was provided
with the scanner driver and more flexible, because its output can be
piped to the PBM tools for scaling, rotation, smoothing and so on.

Thanks to the authors of the Logiscan driver and the gifscan program
for their permission to include parts of their code into PBMSCAN.

PBMSCAN is distributed under the GNU GPL.

Have fun,

Andreas

